Hi María,

My first recommendation is you might want to reinstall RRPP and geomorph using the latest versions of these packages.  We recently updated RRPP to version 2.0.0 and will soon update geomorph, but even without these updates, your versions are behind past updates we have made.  I believe we addressed issues similar to the one you have experienced before, but if you still get the warnings after updating, let me know.

Regardless, if axes are appropriate labeled, this warning is probably innocuous.  It appears to be an attempt to compile 24 components when only 23 are available, but as long as the 23 are returned rather than the analysis arresting because of a error, the warning messages can probably be ignored.

Best,
Mike

