Thank you Mike for your advice last week on reducing the dimensions of the physignal analyses. Now they run perfectly but we came across a new problem.

I extend this question to anyone who might want to pitch in!

In the help tab its mentioned that the preferred Optimization method when you want to maximize effect size (we want to mmake comparisons of z also) is “burn”. We run it first using “mean” and got different results, but as we understand this method may tend to underestimate the phylogenetic signal.

We also want to analyze the profile of K along the components in a similar way as in Collyer and Adams 2021, but when we call the object $K.by.p it says it’s NULL. Shouldn’t it be showing a vector of K?  and we are wondering what could be wrong here….

Thanks in advance to anyone who can help!

